  "worked_solution": "To find every subset of $K,$ we list out every combination of elements within $K.$\n\nWe can use the following diagram to visualize the process:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14114576/assets/ae24126292e3dbf82d714e1e6f4f6bd2a63b44de2534e29e4ca9ad9b26fbe308.png)\n\nNote that we must include the empty set since it is a subset of every set.\n\nBy doing this, we get\n\n$$\n∅,{a},{c},{e},{a,c},{a,e},{c,e},{a,c,e}.\n$$",
